    "updated_at": "2017-06-16T02:03:31Z",
    "body": "Thanks for the explanation. I reread the issues and realized they're discussing play resume, not source change.\r\n\r\nThat said, I'm not sure why this is part of the spec - it seems like less trouble for a developer to reset the playback rate to something default when a track ends, than to track src mutations and restore the playback rate to what it was before as soon as they happen (what I'm doing currently).",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
