    "created_at": "2017-06-16T02:09:41Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-06-16T02:13:59Z",
    "body": "Right - I'm contending, basically, that it's much more implementation trouble to override one default than the other, and the former is the current default. I guess it's probably too late to change it - it's just a shame the only foolproof override (that I've found) requires copying the `playbackRate` to another variable each time it changes.\r\n\r\n```js\r\nvar playbackRate;\r\nmediaElement.addEventListener('ratechange', function() {\r\n  playbackRate = mediaElement.playbackRate;\r\n});\r\nnew MutationObserver(function() {\r\n  mediaElement.playbackRate = playbackRate;\r\n}).observe(mediaElement, {\r\n  attributeFilter: ['src']\r\n});\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhereas the override the other way would be:\r\n```js\r\nmediaElement.addEventListener('ended', function() {\r\n  mediaElement.playbackRate = mediaElement.defaultPlaybackRate;\r\n});\r\n```",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
