    "created_at": "2017-06-16T02:19:17Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-06-16T02:31:47Z",
    "body": "That is actually what I was doing originally, but for the UI library I am developing, I expose the audio element to developers in case they need it as an escape hatch for whatever they're doing, and the UI needs to stay in sync if they screw around with it. It's not really possible to totally anticipate mutations before they happen.\r\n\r\nI'll concede I'm an edge case and writing extra code to sync everything is inevitable.\r\n\r\nI guess a decent proposal (IMO) is to add a boolean property to the media element interface which can be set to override the default behavior. Thoughts?",
    "author_association": "NONE",
