    "created_at": "2017-06-16T02:41:40Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-06-16T02:41:40Z",
    "body": "Well, the whole point is that if a developer specifically resets the src, then they *want* to reset the playback rate; that's what the src API *means*. If they did not want to do that, they would save and restore.\r\n\r\nAs for a new feature proposal, the best way to prove that such a feature is worth the spec, implementation, and test-writing effort for everyone is to release a similar feature as a library, and see how much adoption it gets.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
